			<div class="content" id="post-content-4832632">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: Parasite enters the brain of a human and latches onto certain parts of it encouraging it or forcing it to meet its demands. The parasite spreads via bodily contact with its nesting spot or anybody infected. nesting spots are found within contaminated areas such as sewers, heavily polluted bodies of water. the parasite eventually makes its host practically braindead only able to meet the demands of its master, while the parasite uses the body as a vessel to transmit the parasite and as a food source. the parasite also uses any forms of mental illness and traumatic moments, fond memories, anything that it can find inside the host's mind to exploit.</p>
<p>the parasite uses the researcher to create a document on the parasite claiming that it's not dangerous and that it is beneficial. while writing it, however, consciousness snaps back and he realizes what he is writing and tries to correct it, but with the parasite still in control of his mind, he fails.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: I intend on creating an article that tries to encourage you that the parasite is completely harmless while subtlely explaining what it actually does, while its host tries to fight it off, to no avail</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: the parasite is using humans as hosts to try to encourage others to get themselves infected, specifically via the article</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I would like as much critique as I can get.</p>

